{
  "_comment": [
    "Labelled utterances for the acknowledgement track's [CHAT]/[TASK] classification (orbit/ack.py).",
    "Labels follow the operational definitions in ack._SYSTEM_PROMPT, fixed BEFORE any model run:",
    "  CHAT = the user is only being social or conversational (a greeting, thanks, small talk, a farewell,",
    "         or a question about Orbit itself) and nothing needs doing - no tools, files, browsing or app.",
    "  TASK = anything that has to be done or looked up, however small, including requests wrapped in",
    "         pleasantries, indirect requests ('my screen is too bright') and follow-ups ('do it again').",
    "  AMBIGUOUS = defensible either way (e.g. 'tell me a joke'). Excluded from accuracy; reported only as",
    "              the share routed to TASK, the fail-safe direction.",
    "The set was drafted with an AI assistant from those definitions; the authors should review every label",
    "before quoting results. 'spoken' items imitate raw speech-to-text output: lowercase, fillers, no punctuation.",
    "Contains no personal data. Categories are for stratified reporting only; the classifier never sees them."
  ],
